# One certificate authority of your own, and one entry per service.
#
# `local_certs` is what makes this work without a domain: Caddy signs every
# name below with its own CA instead of asking Let's Encrypt, which would
# require a name you can prove you own. The price is that each device has to
# trust that CA once — see the README.
{
	local_certs
}

# The container name is enough: everything here shares tsdproxy-net, so Caddy
# reaches each service by name on its internal port, with nothing published on
# the LAN.
#
# faved.casa {
#	reverse_proxy faved:80
# }
#
# koffan.casa {
#	reverse_proxy koffan:8080
# }
